-- Plain-language descriptions for the ingredients that had none.
--
-- 316 ingredient names seen on scanned products had no entry at all, and a
-- further 585 bulk-imported E-numbers read "E100 - κουρκουμινη": a name, not
-- an explanation. A shopper reading "Δεν υπάρχει επαληθευμένη περιγραφή" or a
-- bare name learns nothing, so each is given a short factual description in
-- Greek, or an alias onto the entry that already describes it.
--
-- Wording is deliberately neutral: what the substance is and what it does, and
-- a concern only where there is a documented regulatory or health point (EU
-- allergens, contact allergens, saturated fat, sodium, sugars). Nothing here
-- changes a score, except the sweetening ingredients marked below, which join
-- the existing added_sugar rule group (see the note before them).

-- ---- New entries ----
